-- title:
--   Finite and toric parts transport from Jₜop(N₀p) to J₀(N₀p)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $N_0$ and $p$ are natural numbers with $p$ prime and with `hpN₀ : ¬ p ∣ N₀`, and the two divisibility hypotheses `hpM : p ∣ N₀ * p` and `hpM2 : ¬ p ^ 2 ∣ N₀ * p` are imposed; $A$ is a valuation subring of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ satisfying `hA : A.LiesOverPrime p`, that is, $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, and the residue field of $A$ is algebraically closed. The residue field then carries characteristic $p$, and the statement is read with the Hecke-module structures `heckeModuleBar (N₀ * p)` and `heckeModuleBar N₀` on the Picard groups `JZero (N₀ * p)` and `JZero N₀`, and with the algebra structures on `modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField ↥A) N₀` fixed in the preamble.
--
--   **Data on the $\Gamma_\top$ side at level $M = N_0p$.** First, `hj` asserts that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}$-Laurent series generated by the integral-form ratios for the full modular group; $\mathfrak{X}$ is a package `XHDRModelAtP p (N₀ * p) ⊤ hpM hj` of an integral model of the modular curve of level `XHDRLevel.ΓM (N₀ * p) ⊤` over the base ring `R p` (properness, flatness, integrality, finite presentation and normality of the model; a curve model `𝔛.Meta` over the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ with function field `xHFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p) ⊤` together with the identification `𝔛.eeta` of `𝔛.Meta.C` with the geometric generic fibre; Galois compatibility and the chart pinning of the function field; smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre; the cusp sections `𝔛.εinf`, `𝔛.εzero`; and an involution `𝔛.w`). Next, $\theta$ is an automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p) ⊤` over the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$, and `hθ` requires: whenever $f$ in that field and $u$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar ((N₀ * p) / p) (infSubgroup p (N₀ * p) ⊤ hpM)` have the same underlying Laurent series, the Laurent series of $\theta f$ is obtained from that of $u$ by `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) p`, the substitution multiplying exponents by $p$. The hypothesis `hwgen` requires, for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y,y'$ of `𝔛.Meta.C` over the base, that $y'$ followed by `𝔛.eeta`, the first projection and `𝔛.w.hom` being equal to $y$ followed by `𝔛.eeta` and the first projection forces `𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace y' = SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut θ • 𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace y` in the places of `xHFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p) ⊤`. Further, $\rho : R p \to A$ is a ring homomorphism with `hρ` saying that $\rho$ followed by the inclusion of $A$ is the structure map of `R p` into the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$; $\Lambda$ is a `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p (N₀ * p) ⊤ hpM A` and $O$ a `JHNeronObjectAtP p (N₀ * p) ⊤ hpM A hA Λ`, i.e. a smooth separated group scheme `O.G` over `base p` with relative group law `O.L` and a bijection `O.pts` from `JH (N₀ * p) ⊤` onto the sections over `genPt p`. The hypothesis `hD` asserts that the designation $\langle$`O.G`, `O.g`, the unit section of `O.L`$\rangle$ represents, in the sense of `RepresentsRelSubPic`, the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles on `XHDRLevel.toBase p (XHDRLevel.ΓM (N₀ * p) ⊤) hj` rigidified along `𝔛.εinf` which are fibrewise algebraically trivial (`algEquivZeroCut`). Finally `hΛ` asserts `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle (baseRing p) Λ.f` (smoothness, properness, connected fibres and existence of a relative group law for `Λ.f`), and `hσ` that `Λ.σA` is the morphism induced by $\rho$.
--
--   **The Abel–Jacobi bridge on the $\Gamma_\top$ side.** There are given: `hDQT`, the same representability statement after base change of the model to $\mathbb{Q}$, for the base-changed designation and the base-changed cusp section; a separatedness hypothesis for the generic fibre; a section `ajQT` of the base-changed designation over the base-changed curve; a morphism `kQT` from the fibre over `genPt p` to the fibre over `specMap (R p) ℚ`; a morphism `ajbarT : 𝔛.Meta.C ⟶ O.G`; and a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point `εbarT` of `𝔛.Meta.C` over the base. The hypothesis `HAJ` is the conjunction of eleven clauses: (1) the Poincaré bundle of `hDQT` is isomorphic to the base change to $\mathbb{Q}$ of the Poincaré bundle of `hD` pulled back along the first projection of the fibre product of `O.g` with `specMap (R p) ℚ`; (2) the base-changed cusp section followed by `ajQT` is the zero section of the base-changed designation; (3) for every field $K$, every morphism $t$ from $\operatorname{Spec} K$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$ and every point $x$ of the base-changed curve over $t$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDQT` along $x$ followed by `ajQT` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $t$ followed by the base-changed cusp section; (4) and (5) `kQT` is compatible with the two projections, the second up to the map $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$; (6) `ajbarT` is `𝔛.eeta` followed by `kQT`, `ajQT` and the first projection; (7) `ajbarT` followed by `O.g` is `𝔛.Meta.toBase` followed by `genPt p`; (8) `εbarT` followed by `𝔛.eeta` and the first projection is `genPt p` followed by `𝔛.εinf`; (9) `εbarT` followed by `ajbarT` is `genPt p` followed by the unit section of `O.L`; (10) `O.pts` is additive for the relative group law attached to `hD` through `algEquivZeroGroupCut`; (11) for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x,s$ of `𝔛.Meta.C` over the base with $s$ sitting over the cusp section `𝔛.εinf` in the sense of (8), there exists a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on `xHFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p) ⊤` equal to the difference of the points of the places of $x$ and of $s$, such that `(O.pts (Pic0.mk Dv)).1` is $x$ followed by `ajbarT`.
--
--   **Data and bridge hypothesis on the $J_0$ side.** For every level datum `Λ₀ : JZeroNeronObjectAtP.LevelData N₀ p A` satisfying the seven-clause predicate `Λ₀.IsJacobian` (that `Λ₀.f` satisfies the abelian-scheme property bundle over `baseRing p`; commutativity of its group law on points; additivity of `Λ₀.pts` and of `Λ₀.ptsSp`; Galois equivariance of `Λ₀.pts`; a compatibility of reduction of points under `ReductionInputsModL A N₀`; and the realisation of each element of the Hecke algebra by an endomorphism of `Λ₀.f` over the base), every `O₀ : JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ₀` and every model package `𝔓 : DRModelPackageLevel N₀ p hpN₀` for `DRLevel.X N₀ p` over `R p`, the following hypothesis — the conclusion of the existence-and-bridge statement on the $J_0$ side, a conjunction of three blocks — is assumed.
--
--   The first block asserts the existence, for the designation $D = \langle$`O₀.G`, `O₀.g`, the unit section of `O₀.L`$\rangle$ over `toBase N₀ p`, of: a representability datum `hD` for the fibrewise algebraically trivial rigidified Picard subfunctor rigidified along `𝔓.εinf`; the corresponding datum `hDQ` after base change to $\mathbb{Q}$; an isomorphism `hPQ` of the Poincaré bundle of `hDQ` with the base change of that of `hD` pulled back along the first projection; a separatedness hypothesis for the base change to $\mathbb{Q}$; a section `ajQ` with `hajQε` (the base-changed cusp section followed by `ajQ` is the zero section) and `hajQ` (the clause of type (3) above, for all fields $K$, all $t$ and all $K$-points $x$); a morphism `kQ` with the two compatibilities `hkQ₁`, `hkQ₂`; a morphism `ajbar : 𝔓.Meta.C ⟶ D.P` with `hajbar` identifying it as `𝔓.eeta` followed by `kQ`, `ajQ` and the first projection, and `hajbar_over` placing it over `𝔓.Meta.toBase` followed by `genPt p`; and a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point `εbar` of `𝔓.Meta.C` with `hεbar` (it lies over `𝔓.εinf`) and `hεbar_aj` (it is carried by `ajbar` to the zero section) — such that `O₀.pts` is additive for the relative group law attached to `hD`, and such that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x,s$ of `𝔓.Meta.C` with $s$ lying over `𝔓.εinf` there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p)` equal to the difference of the points of the places of $x$ and of $s$ with `(O₀.pts (Pic0.mk Dv)).1` equal to $x$ followed by `ajbar`.
--
--   The second block asserts the existence of: a ring homomorphism $\rho : R p \to A$ compatible with the structure map to the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ and with `Λ₀.σA` induced by $\rho$; modular polynomial data `data : ModularPolynomialData p` (a monic $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(p)$ annihilating the pair $(j, j_p)$ of $q$-expansions) satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr` (the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $p$ is $(X^p - Y)(X - Y^p)$ in the bivariate normalisation used); integrality hypotheses `hα`, `hβ` for the two degeneracy embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` at level $N_0$ and prime $p$; a place specialisation $P$ over the residue field of $A$ along its residue map composed with $\rho$; a prolongation tuple `Rt` for $P$ satisfying `Rt.IsModel`, `Rt.RegularityLaw O₀.ssFinset`, `Rt.NodeValueLaw O₀.ssFinset` and `Rt.OrderLawFixed`; a homomorphism `sp` from the inertia invariants `inertiaInvariants A (N₀ * p)` of `JZero (N₀ * p)` to the glued Picard group `GluedPic0` of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField ↥A) N₀` relative to the node pairs `nodePairsOfPlaces (arithFrobC p (ResidueField ↥A) N₀) O₀.ssFinset`, with `P.IsGluedSpecialization` for that finset and `sp`; and an equality `hE` of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField ↥A) N₀` with `modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField ↥A) N₀` — such that six statements hold: `O₀.frob` is the coefficientwise Frobenius semilinear automorphism `arithFrobC p (ResidueField ↥A) N₀`; two reduction clauses, stating that for every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $y$ of `𝔓.Meta.C` over the base, every point $u$ of the model over the morphism induced by $\rho$ whose $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-specialisation agrees with $y$ through `𝔓.eeta` and the first projection, every morphism $u_\kappa$ from the spectrum of the residue field into the fibre of the model along the residue map composed with $\rho$ subject to the two stated compatibilities, under the alternative that the place of $y$ satisfies `P.IsStrictFst` or `P.IsStrictSnd`, and every closed point of the special-fibre curve model `𝔓.Mfib` whose image under `𝔓.efib` is the image of the closed point under $u_\kappa$ followed by `fibreMap0 𝔓.π` (respectively under $u_\kappa$ followed by `fibreMap 𝔓.w.hom 𝔓.w_over` and then `fibreMap0 𝔓.π`), the place of that closed point is `P.reduceFst` (respectively `P.reduceSnd`) of the place of $y$; for every inertia-invariant class $x$, the section `O₀.pts x` extends over $A$ in the sense of `ExtendsToPlace A Λ₀.σA` if and only if `P.IsGoodClass` holds for $x$ and the above node pairs; for every inertia-invariant $x$ and every section $s$ over `Λ₀.σA` with `(O₀.pts x).1` equal to the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $A$ followed by $s$, the pair obtained by transporting along the inverse of `Pic0.congr` for `hE` the inverses under `Λ₀.ptsSp` of the two branch specialisations `fibreMap (O₀.abqFibre 0) …` and `fibreMap (O₀.abqFibre 1) …` of $s$ equals `GluedPic0.toPic0Pair` of `sp x`; and, for the same $x$ and $s$, the specialisation of $s$ factors through the torus `torusStr (ResidueField ↥A) O₀.toricRank` via `O₀.torusFibre` if and only if `GluedPic0.toPic0Pair` of `sp x` vanishes.
--
--   The third block consists of the two inertia clauses: for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` and every $x$ in the $m$-torsion `jZeroTorsion (N₀ * p) m`, the difference $\sigma \cdot x - x$ lies in `O₀.toricPts m`; and for every $m > 0$, every such $\sigma$ and every such $x$, that difference lies in `O₀.finPts m`.
--
--   **Comparison data.** Assuming in addition `hF`, an equality of `xHFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p) ⊤` with `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p)` as subfields of the Laurent series over the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$; an isomorphism $\varphi$ of `XHDRLevel.X p (XHDRLevel.ΓM (N₀ * p) ⊤) hj` with `DRLevel.X N₀ p` such that $\varphi$ followed by `DRLevel.toBase N₀ p` is `XHDRLevel.toBase p (XHDRLevel.ΓM (N₀ * p) ⊤) hj`, such that `𝔛.εinf` followed by $\varphi$ is `𝔓.εinf`, and such that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y$ of `𝔛.Meta.C` and $y_0$ of `𝔓.Meta.C` over their bases with $y$ followed by `𝔛.eeta`, the first projection and $\varphi$ equal to $y_0$ followed by `𝔓.eeta` and the first projection, the place of $y_0$ is the transport along `hF` (via `Place.congrRingEquiv`) of the place of $y$; and finally an additive isomorphism $e$ from `JH (N₀ * p) ⊤` to `JZero (N₀ * p)` which agrees pointwise with `Pic0.congr` of the ring equivalence given by `hF`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $m > 0$ both of the following hold: the image of `O.finPts m` under $e$ equals `O₀.finPts m`, and the image of `O.toricPts m` under $e$ equals `O₀.toricPts m`. Here `O.finPts m` is the subgroup of `JH (N₀ * p) ⊤` generated by those $m$-torsion classes $x$ of `Pic0` for which the section `O.pts x` extends over $A$ along `Λ.σA`, and `O₀.finPts m` is the analogous subgroup of `JZero (N₀ * p)` formed from `jZeroTorsion (N₀ * p) m` and `Λ₀.σA`; `O.toricPts m` and `O₀.toricPts m` are the subgroups generated by the ranges of the respective toric points `O.toricPoint m` and `O₀.toricPoint m` (and are trivial for $m = 0$).
--
--   This is the level-comparison step identifying the two pieces of the Néron filtration — the classes whose sections extend over the valuation ring $A$ above $p$ (the finite part) and the toric part — for the Néron object of $J_\top(N_0p)$ with those for the Néron object of $J_0(N_0p)$, along the identification of the two Deligne–Rapoport integral models and of their function fields at $H = \top$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.toricFrobeniusHecke_toricMonodromyPart_jZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.toricFrobeniusHecke_toricMonodromyPart_jZero), in the analysis of the action of Frobenius and of the Hecke operators on the toric monodromy part at $p$.
